%N A398195 Semiprimes p*q such that p^2*q is a triangular number.
%C A398195 It is not required that p < q.
%C A398195 Consists of 57, p*(2*p^2-1) for p in A106483, and p*(p^2 + 1)/2 for p in A048161. - _Robert Israel_, Jul 23 2026
%H A398195 Robert Israel, <a href="/A398195/b398195.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%e A398195 14 is a term because 7*2*2=28 is a triangular number: 28=7*8/2.
%p A398195 N:= 10^9: # for terms <= N
%p A398195 R:= 57: p:= 1:
%p A398195 do
%p A398195   p:= nextprime(p);
%p A398195 if p*(2*p^2-1) > N then break fi;
%p A398195   if isprime(2*p^2-1) then R:= R, p*(2*p^2-1) fi
%p A398195 od:
%p A398195 p:= 2:
%p A398195 do
%p A398195   p:= nextprime(p);
%p A398195 if p*(p^2+1)/2 > N then break fi;
%p A398195 if isprime((p^2+1)/2) then R:= R, p*(p^2+1)/2 fi
%p A398195 od:
%p A398195 sort([R]); # _Robert Israel_, Jul 23 2026
%o A398195 (Python)
%o A398195 from sympy import factorint, integer_nthroot
%o A398195 def istri(n): return integer_nthroot(8*n+1, 2)[1]
%o A398195 def ok(k): return sum((f:=factorint(k)).values()) == 2 and any(istri(p*k) for p in f)
%o A398195 print([k for k in range(10**6) if ok(k)]) # _Michael S. Branicky_, Jul 23 2026
%o A398195 (PARI) isok(k) = if (bigomega(k)==2, my(f=factor(k)); if (#f~ == 1, ispolygonal(k^3, 3), ispolygonal(k*f[1,1], 3) || ispolygonal(k*f[2,1], 3))); \\ _Michel Marcus_, Jul 23 2026
%Y A398195 Cf. A000217, A001358, A010054, A075875, A292989.
